= Proof-or-Stop:Don’t Trust the Agent, Trust the Evidence Loop Engineering for Verifiable Evidence-Gated Lifecycle Control

Lifecycle transitions (reviewed, tested, done, ready-to-merge) stay mere agent claims unless a downstream system can check them against evidence. Proof-or-Stop admits a transition only when fresh, source-state-bound, mechanically verifiable evidence satisfies the gate — agent outputs may propose lifecycle claims but never constitute them. In a 9,240-cell ablation it cut visible-pass/hidden-fail amplification from 31/1800 to 2/1800, and a self-hosted corpus (565 stories, 94.8% of review findings resolved) shows the system producing auditable evidence on its own development.
